{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "ProdMesh Graphics \u2014 control API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "The documented control surface. **This is the only real surface**; every other one \u2014 Companion, RossTalk, DashBoard, GPI, OSC, MIDI \u2014 is a thin adapter over it, and if an adapter needs something this cannot express, the API grows (control-surfaces.md \u00a71).\n\n## Two hosts, one shape\n\nThe control server on `:8519` owns content and assignment. Each playout node also serves `POST /cue` on `:8520` with the **same body**, and that one keeps working when the server is down \u2014 which is why GPI, OSC and MIDI terminate there. An adapter changes a host, not a payload.\n\n## The take button must never lie\n\n`POST /api/cue` is **synchronous**. It does not return until the node confirms or the deadline expires. A 2xx means it is on air; anything else says why in `label`, as a sentence meant to be shown to an operator verbatim.\n\n## Four results that mean different things\n\n`applied` fired. `deduped` was the same action arriving twice \u2014 the mechanism working. `superseded` was replaced by a newer take for the same layers before it fired (ADR 0017). `rejected` did not fire, and `reason` says why. A panel with three lamps needs `superseded` and a late `rejected` to light different ones.\n\n## cue_id is the caller's responsibility\n\nGenerate it **where the human acted** \u2014 at button-press, at key-down, at the GPI edge \u2014 and reuse it on retry. It is carried unchanged to the node, which dedupes on it. A client that mints a fresh id per retry has defeated the mechanism, so a missing one is a 422 rather than something the server invents."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "http://localhost:8519",
      "description": "Control server"
    },
    {
      "url": "http://localhost:8520",
      "description": "Playout node \u2014 /cue and /status only, works with the server down"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "cue",
      "description": "Putting graphics on air. The operative surface."
    },
    {
      "name": "rundown",
      "description": "The running order and the operator's place in it."
    },
    {
      "name": "content",
      "description": "Templates and Items."
    },
    {
      "name": "nodes",
      "description": "Playout nodes and their outputs."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/api/cue": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "cue"
        ],
        "operationId": "cue",
        "summary": "Take, take out, update, clear",
        "description": "Synchronous: returns when the node confirms or the deadline expires.\n\n**A partly-delivered take returns 503**, not 207, carrying `result: \"partial\"` and a per-destination breakdown. Deliberately a failure status with success detail: the take button must not go green unless everything fired, and a client checking only `res.ok` goes green on any 2xx.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CueRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Applied, deduped, or superseded.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CueResult"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No such node.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Rejected by the node, not adopted, or no such item.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Missing cue_id, unknown op, or nothing to do.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "Node offline, no confirmation, or **partly delivered**.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/cue/batch": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "cue"
        ],
        "operationId": "cueBatch",
        "summary": "Several cues as one look",
        "description": "Stops at the first failure. Half a look is worse than none.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "cues"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "cues": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CueRequest"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Every cue applied."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Stopped partway; `results` holds what did fire.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/cuelog": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "cue"
        ],
        "operationId": "cueLog",
        "summary": "What fired, in order",
        "description": "`?since=<seq>` recovers a gap. Events reach a browser as the snapshot of this log's tail, never as bare frames on a conflating topic (ADR 0008).",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "show",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "default": "default"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "since",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Entries after `since`."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/rundowns/{id}/cursor": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "rundown"
        ],
        "operationId": "getCursor",
        "summary": "Where the operator is",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The cursor."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No such rundown.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "put": {
        "tags": [
          "rundown"
        ],
        "operationId": "moveCursor",
        "summary": "Move, jump to an item, or jump to a section",
        "description": "**Navigation only \u2014 this never takes anything.** Show composes a cursor move and a cue into one button because that is what an operator wants; keeping them separate here is what lets the UI show 'the rundown is here, the output is showing something else' instead of pretending they cannot differ.\n\n`section` resolves to that section's FIRST entry \u2014 going back to the chorus means starting it again.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "delta": {
                    "type": "integer"
                  },
                  "item": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "section": {
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The new cursor."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No such rundown.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Not in this rundown, or nothing to move by.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/rundowns": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "rundown"
        ],
        "operationId": "listRundowns",
        "summary": "Every rundown",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Every rundown"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/playlists": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "rundown"
        ],
        "operationId": "listPlaylists",
        "summary": "Every playlist",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Every playlist"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/items": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "content"
        ],
        "operationId": "listItems",
        "summary": "Every Item",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Every Item"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/templates": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "content"
        ],
        "operationId": "listTemplates",
        "summary": "Every template",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Every template"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/nodes": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "nodes"
        ],
        "operationId": "listNodes",
        "summary": "Every node, with what it reports on air",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Every node, with what it reports on air"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/health": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "nodes"
        ],
        "operationId": "health",
        "summary": "Server and node health",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Server and node health"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/version": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "nodes"
        ],
        "operationId": "version",
        "summary": "Server version",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Server version"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/rundowns/{id}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "rundown"
        ],
        "operationId": "getRundown",
        "summary": "One rundown: its playlists, their modes and sections, and the cursor",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The rundown."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No such rundown.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/stream": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "nodes"
        ],
        "operationId": "stream",
        "summary": "Server-sent events for snapshot topics",
        "description": "`?topics=a,b`. Every topic here is **snapshot-shaped and conflates**: the newest frame supersedes every earlier one completely. Cues are NOT delivered this way \u2014 a superseded event is a lost event. Use `/api/cuelog` (ADR 0008).",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "topics",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "An SSE stream."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/cue": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "cue"
        ],
        "operationId": "nodeCue",
        "summary": "The same cue, submitted to a node directly (port 8520)",
        "description": "**Works with the control server down**, which is why GPI, OSC and MIDI terminate here (ADR 0014). Same body as `/api/cue`, so an adapter changes a host rather than a payload.\n\nOps are a subset \u2014 `take`, `take_out`, `clear_layer`, `clear_all`, `arm` \u2014 because `update` needs bound data and `timeline` needs a name and an action, and a contact closure has neither.\n\n**No authentication.** A booth LAN with no internet, and a credential check against a server that is down is a lock with no key.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CueRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Applied, deduped, or superseded.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CueResult"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Rejected by the engine; `reason` says why.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "No cue_id, or an op this surface does not take.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "The engine did not confirm.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Problem"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/status": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "nodes"
        ],
        "operationId": "nodeStatus",
        "summary": "What a node has on air (port 8520)",
        "description": "The node is the authority for this (ADR 0009), so it is the answer rather than a cache of one \u2014 which is why it is worth having when the server has failed.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Outputs, layers, and occupants."
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "schemas": {
      "Problem": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Every failure. `label` is a complete sentence written for an operator and is meant to be shown verbatim rather than reworded.",
        "required": [
          "error",
          "label"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Stable machine code."
          },
          "label": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The sentence to show."
          }
        }
      },
      "CueRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "cue_id",
          "op"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "cue_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Minted where the human acted; reused on retry. See the dedupe note."
          },
          "op": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "take",
              "take_also",
              "take_out",
              "arm",
              "update",
              "clear_layer",
              "clear_all",
              "preload",
              "timeline"
            ]
          },
          "item": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Required by take, take_also, arm and preload."
          },
          "node": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Omit on a take to fan to every node the Item lives on (ADR 0018). Naming one takes to that node alone \u2014 the escape hatch when a machine is having a bad morning."
          },
          "output": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "layer": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "By NAME, never by index: an index silently re-points at a different graphic the moment someone reorders the stack."
          },
          "data": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "description": "update only. Rebinds a live graphic and morphs to the new layout."
          },
          "tween_ms": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "update only. 0 is a hard cut \u2014 correcting a misspelled name should not be a 400 ms animation about itself."
          },
          "deadline_ms": {
            "type": "integer",
            "default": 500,
            "description": "A take past its deadline is REJECTED, not fired late. A graphic four seconds after the button is worse than one that never appears."
          },
          "surface": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "show_view",
              "companion",
              "rosstalk",
              "gpi",
              "osc",
              "midi",
              "api",
              "node_local"
            ],
            "description": "Recorded on every cue-log entry. Without it the log is confusing the first time someone uses a GPI."
          },
          "show": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "default"
          }
        }
      },
      "CueResult": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "result": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "applied",
              "deduped",
              "superseded",
              "partial"
            ]
          },
          "fired_at_frame": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "description": "The output frame the graphic went on. Not the frame of the request."
          },
          "seq": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Cue-log sequence, for ?since= gap recovery."
          },
          "label": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "destinations": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DestinationResult"
            },
            "description": "Present when a take fanned to more than one node."
          }
        }
      },
      "DestinationResult": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "node": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "result": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "detail": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
